[<p><b>This position is open until filled; however, the initial review of applications will begin on October 19, 2018.</b><br/>
<br/>
<b>This is a full-time, long-term temporary position through December 2019. The position is partially grant funded and may be renewable into 2020 and beyond.</b><br/>
<br/>
King County Housing Authority (KCHA), an independent municipal organization, is a high performing nationally recognized leader in affordable housing. KCHA provides innovative and effective housing solutions so that people and communities can prosper. Our vision is that all residents of King County have quality affordable housing. KCHA is the largest housing provider in the county, and annually, the agency serves over 50,000 low-income individuals.<br/>
<br/>
The Department of Policy and Research promotes effective and innovative policies and programs throughout KCHA. We work across departments and systems to engage in rigorous research, design, evaluation, and analysis in support of KCHA's mission, as well as to advance the local and national evidence-base on affordable housing and related areas.<br/>
<br/>
For more information about KCHA, visit www.kcha.org.<br/>
<br/>
<b>ABOUT THE POSITION:</b><br/>
The Policy and Research Department is currently seeking a full-time Research &amp; Data Analyst to support the Department's research, analysis, and data management efforts. This is a unique opportunity to engage in meaningful, applied research and analysis on housing and social policy. The Analyst will assist in a variety of tasks and projects across the Department and agency, and will get to work on a variety of policy areas and analytic approaches.<br/>
<br/>
This position is partially grant funded that may be renewable into 2020 and beyond.</p>, <p>The Research &amp; Data Analyst work will involve:</p>, <ul>
<li>Analysis of agency administrative data, both for regular reporting efforts and in response to emergent requests;
</li><li>Preparation of data extracts and matched data sets;
</li><li>Creation and updating of data utilization tools, including reports, dashboards, and quality assurance tracking tools;
</li><li>Literature review and syntheses of best practices;
</li><li>Participation in qualitative and/or quantitative data collection and management processes including tool development, fieldwork, and data cleaning;
</li><li>Development of data reports, visualizations, and/or other briefing materials to effectively convey findings to intended stakeholders.</li></ul>, <p><b>Required Qualifications:</b></p>, <ul>
<li>Associate's Degree with degrees preferred in public administration, public policy, sociology, community development, or related field <b>AND </b>three years of experience in housing programs, community development or social services <b>OR</b> an equivalent combination of education and experience.</li></ul>, <ul>
<li>Experience in qualitative and qualitative research applications including data collection, management, and analysis;
</li><li>Outstanding Excel skills and strong proficiencies in other MS applications;
</li><li>Strong critical thinking skills and an ability to introduce creative problem-solving to complex analytic puzzles;
</li><li>Knowledge of affordable housing policy and research and/or knowledge of related social policy arenas such as health, education, or other areas;
</li><li>Experience working with large and/or administrative datasets strongly preferred;
</li><li>Knowledge and skill in using analytic software programs such as Stata, Tableau, or GIS;
</li><li>Knowledge and ability in creating reports, dashboard, and other data summary and visualization materials;
</li><li>Strong organizational skills including the ability to handle multiple projects simultaneously;
</li><li>Exceptional written and verbal communication skills;
</li><li>Collaborative team player that is at ease working with multiple and diverse stakeholders and who brings enthusiasm, curiosity, humility, and humor to their work.</li></ul>, <ul>
<li>Consent to and pass required assessments.
</li><li>Consent to and pass a criminal records background check.</li></ul>, <p><b>Application Requirements:</b><br/>
To be considered for this opportunity, you must:</p>, <ul>
<li>Complete the online application profile in its entirety.
</li><li>Upload a cover letter that addresses how your experience and education qualifies you to perform the functions listed in the job announcement. <b>(Cover Letter)</b>
</li><li>Upload a detailed résumé of all educational and professional experience. <b>(Résumé)</b></li></ul>]

[<p>The Quality Data Analyst supports data analytics strategies across the organization, as well as participating in the development of new business intelligence solutions. The Quality Data Analyst provides quality assurance of reports generated for internal and external distribution and validates compliance with corporate, contractual, and regulatory guidelines. The Quality Data Analyst uses analytical skills to monitor key performance indicators and provide actionable data for business decision purposes. The incumbent will work directly with organizational leadership to bring actionable insights, enable data-driven decision-making and create a culture of sustainment. The Quality Data Analyst also helps coordinate the hospital’s core measure compliance program.</p>, <p>Bachelor’s degree (Master’s Degree preferred) in business management, finance, mathematics, engineering technology, nursing or health care management.<br/>
<br/>
Experience: Current experience in hospital-based setting and knowledge of regulatory requirements (i.e., The Joint Commission, DOH, IPRO, CMS) is preferred. Proficiency in desktop computer and statistical applications is required. Excellent written and interpersonal communication skills, demonstrated leadership and facilitation skills are essential for this role.</p>, <ul><li>Organizes the hospitals core measures compliance program including compliance assessment, record abstraction, data analysis, data submission to state, national and accrediting entities and staff/MD education;
</li><li>Quality
 • Data abstraction, summarization, and reporting to various leadership levels throughout the organization across the following domains:
 o Quality Assurance
 o Patient Safety
 o Risk Management
 o Regulatory Compliance
 o Infection Control
 o Value Based Purchasing
</li><li>Remains well-informed of current trends in technology and best practice as it relates to Healthcare Quality, High Reliability, and Excellence in Patient Care Services<br/>
</li><li>Project Management
 • Facilitates performance improvement through Lean methodologies; identifying, designing and evaluating performance improvement initiatives.
 o Works directly with key stakeholders to operationalize plans into actions;
 o Continuously evaluates initiatives and actively leads solutions;
 o Collaborates with leaders to develop and reinforce metrics for improvement opportunities.
 • Manages project time lines.
</li><li>Data Analysis
 • Identify short and long term business strategies through analytics;
 • Research data anomalies and engage business and operational stakeholders to develop solutions;
 • Monitor critical key performance indicators, such as Value Based Purchasing (VBP), and engage appropriate stakeholders to drive improvement actions;
 • Perform quality assurance functions as they relate to reporting and data validation;
 • Analyze and interpret data for business and operational initiatives;
 • Oversee ad-hoc and operational reports.
</li><li>Proactively and independently assesses data needs for the Quality Services Department and as a liaison for Quality Services Department to the organizational quality data needs.
</li><li>Patient Experience
 • Assists department leaders in identifying and addressing operational issues which impact patient satisfaction;
 • Maintains up-to-date knowledge of regional and national benchmarks, survey tools and customer service initiatives.
</li><li>Assists in enhancing the performance improvement information system(s) and its data collection and reporting tools;
</li><li>Interprets and communicates the organizations performance specific to external quality reports and scorecards;
</li><li>Assists in the investigative activities for the risk management program;
</li><li>Ensures selected organizational and departmental performance measures support regulatory standards and strategic initiatives;
</li><li>Leadership
 • Works directly with the Director of Quality and Quality Services Department to further develop leadership skills in service excellence, change management, quality assurance, and Lean methodologies;
 • Demonstrates commitment within and across multi-disciplinary teams;
 • Works directly as an active member of an interdisciplinary team;
 • Cultivates engagement and commitment across interdisciplinary teams;
 • Demonstrates an ability to quickly adapt to change;
 • Effectively communicates within a large and diverse organization.
 Knowledge
 • Researches, stays informed of and shares best practices from the healthcare industry, project management/performance improvement methodology and operations;
 • Actively seeks educational opportunities- attending seminars and conferences related to Quality and Healthcare.</li><li>
Provides support the infection prevention program for the health system;
</li><li>Organization of data for Ongoing Professional Practice Evaluation, Focused Professional Practice Evaluation, and the Peer Review Process.
</li><li>Skills &amp; Abilities
 • Ability to fully understand business goals and metrics and translate requirements into actionable analysis.
 • Well-developed ability to assess trends and insight from multiple data sets and large amounts of data, using text and statistical analytics, advanced Excel and other statistical and analytics solutions.
 • Detail-oriented and results driven with a passion for producing high-quality deliverables.
 • Demonstrated expertise in data visualization tools and business intelligence platforms.
 • Demonstrated expertise in building, mentoring, and achieving high performing teams.
 • Have the ability to turn data into insight, and to think creatively.
 • Strong analytical skills, excellent communication skills and the ability to communicate actionable analytical findings to a non-technical audience in clear and concise language.
 • Proven ability to frame a business issue, design the right solution, and deliver results.
 • Ability to lead projects and teams.
 • Exposure to / experience working with large data sets.</li></ul>]

[<p>As a key member of an Agile development and/or support team, the Senior Data Engineer performs technical design, development, modification, implementation, maintenance and support of applications using existing and emerging technologies such as Microsoft SSIS ETL, SQL Server, Data Warehousing and Data Integration. With minimal supervision, analyzes business needs and delivers high quality SSIS ETL codes in a U.S. healthcare software environment.
</p>, <p><b>Responsibilities:</b></p>, <ul>
<li>Supports and improves current implementations for our proprietary healthcare software data applications and systems</li>
<li>Enhances and supports automated testing and assist in design as needed;</li>
<li>Oversees the delivery of business priorities in a Scaled Agile Framework (SAFe) environment;
</li><li>Designs, deploys, enhances, tests, automates and supports advanced software solutions;
</li><li>Acts as an implementation logic expert for assigned business applications;
</li><li>Trains and mentors junior level developers;
</li><li>Improves technical design and implementation of the business applications to reduce technical debt;
</li><li>Creates, optimizes and supports MS SQL stored procedures and optimizes existing SSIS packages;
</li><li>Leverages Test Driven Development, Test Automation and Continuous Delivery practices and works with advanced ETL topics such as Data Warehousing and Slowly Changing Dimensions, and Healthcare EDI formats and processes;
</li><li>Daily use of: Team Foundation Server, SSIS, TSQL, SQL Server 2008 &amp; 2016, and SSAS A Plus, Source Control Management tools.
</li></ul>, <p><br/>
<b>Requirements:</b></p>, <ul>
<li>Bachelor’s degree in Computer Science, Engineering, or equivalent</li>
<li>7 - 10 years experience developing complex software applications using ETL, TSQL, SQL Server 2008+ and SSIS
</li><li>Experience in an Agile environment.</li></ul>]
